1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,850
Why does visual thinking make learning so

2
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:05,225
much easier? Let's break it down.

3
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:09,551
Text requires sequential decoding. You have to read words

4
00:00:09,651 --> 00:00:12,733
one by one just to build a mental picture.

5
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:17,933
But with visuals, your brain processes the relationships immediately.

6
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:22,133
This leads to instant recognition of the core concept.

7
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:24,583
Now let's talk about speed.

8
00:00:26,683 --> 00:00:30,383
While reading text takes time and effort to absorb...

9
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:34,208
Visuals are processed almost instantaneously.

10
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,182
In fact, the brain processes images up

11
00:00:37,282 --> 00:00:40,400
to sixty thousand times faster than text.

12
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,375
Finally, how well do we remember it?

13
00:00:45,483 --> 00:00:50,033
People typically remember only 20 percent of what they read...

14
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:54,033
...but they retain up to 80 percent of what they see and do.

15
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:57,758
So, don't just read it. See it, and learn it faster.

